    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Creating sessions with 'mini.sessions' should be done via [`MiniSessions.write()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/691c5f38f575b572d0c857bd22c35be9a1512925/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L146), not the built-in `:mksession`. `MiniSessions.write()` explicitly requires session name: if it is equal to the `config.file`, then file will be created locally, otherwise - in `config.directory` for global sessions. You can also take a look at [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/33#discussioncomment-4894341) with a bit more details about workflow.",
